"""INFRA-04 mandatory gate runner: G01..G54 (assignment §03).

Two phases, one report:

* the **runtime phase** (this module) executes G01..G52 and records the
  external-review requirement G54, driving a live deployment of the exact
  accepted artifact through the eighteen drills;
* the **package phase** (:mod:`scripts.infra04.preseal`) executes G53
  against the final archive bytes and merges the complete 54-gate report.

Anti-cheat rules that hold everywhere in this module:

* every evidence document is regenerated by this run — a stale file from an
  earlier run is never reused, and the run writes before it reads;
* every verdict comes from an observation made in this process, not from a
  description of one;
* the only four verdicts are ``PASS``, ``FAIL``, ``BLOCKED`` and
  ``NOT_APPLICABLE_GOVERNED``. There is no "pass with environment
  limitation": a gate that cannot execute is ``BLOCKED`` and blocks the
  seal;
* the runner never emits ``AUTHORITATIVE_RESULT`` and never claims
  acceptance, production readiness, certification or INFRA-layer closure.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from datetime import UTC, datetime
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

from scripts.acceptance.canonical import seal_document, sha256_file
